# armour/man/sash: the SASH over-layer (STYLE_P2 28.3 over-layer; contracts 3c.1 `role overlay sash`): a 2 px band in the
# people's colour (Accent) from the right shoulder across the chest to the left hip, lit on its upper edge (p), its body (o),
# its shaded lower edge (n); a knot on the hip over the belt and two 2 px tails hanging three rows over the fauld, a dark
# fold (m) between them; R on the tails' hem (T5 gilt). It crosses OVER the chest motif (torso z 4, the motif at z 3).
# Facing up the band runs from the other shoulder to the belt (no knot behind); the side views show it over the shoulder.
# FORGE-TORSO round 2 i1 (generated by the area's tools/gen_sash.py). Format: rpg/art/doll/doll.h.
# (FORGE-TORSO round 2 i3) facing D the band carries a dark edge (m) on its upper side too, so the lit band sits between
# two dark lines and reads as a stripe in greyscale at 1x (the panel: 'the sash doesn't show').
use person
body man
role overlay sash
layer torso
anchor neck
keys torso
z 4
tags overlay

